				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sinn1sl0ken" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2019868); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2019868&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607028005" alt="sinn1sl0ken" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2019868)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sinn1sl0ken" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2019868); return false;" >sinn1sl0ken</a></span> <span class="odate time_1494442076 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 May 2017 18:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2816802">
									

<p>I like the core idea, the development of the product, the insight into the process via email chain (fitting for the Anderson Robotics setting, and I feel as if I've seen similar flavor in Anderson tales before), and the logs give it another level of content that puts more focus on what sapient toys might think about in their spare time.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Nitpick&nbsp;enclosed</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Damn&nbsp;you're&nbsp;too&nbsp;nitpicky</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I do think that choosing to have DM overhear the theological conversation in log 3 seems a little heavy handed, however. Johnny seems to understand the concept of theodicy instantly and well enough to talk about it, so it seems the other dolls would be capable of eventually coming to the same conclusions.</p>
<p>Having an otherwise extraneous character mention the concept just inside earshot and having Leo act upon it the very next day is a little convenient for me (I'm surprised Leo came to philosophical grips with the concept so quickly as well). Were Leo's actions be spurred by gradual unease with his unnatural toy and then having DM contextualize theodicy in terms of the D&amp;D campaign they were playing together would make it feel a touch less contrived to me.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>That being said, that's a very minor quibble with an article I very much liked for multiple reasons right off the bat. Enthusiastic +1.</p>

							</div>

								
					
